// The strafe (right) vector: forward rotated -90 degrees, i.e.
// (cos(yaw), -sin(yaw)) -- see fwd.id's derivation comment. Only its x lives
// here: right.z is exactly -sin(yaw)*speed, the same value fwd.x computes
// (rotating 90 degrees swaps and sign-flips the axes), so strafing reads that
// z from fwd_dx() rather than keeping a second function that only forwards to it.

right_dx() {
  int ps_get_v = (import ps)[2];
  int ret_i = fx_cos_deg(ps_get_v) * (import move_speed) / 1000;
} return int ret_i;
